     |      with multi-level columns, as the stacked dataframe typically
     |      has more values than the original dataframe. Missing values
     |      are filled with NaNs:
     |
     |      >>> df_multi_level_cols2
     |          weight height
     |              kg      m
     |      cat    1.0    2.0
     |      dog    3.0    4.0
     |      >>> df_multi_level_cols2.stack()
     |              weight  height
     |      cat kg     1.0     NaN
     |          m      NaN     2.0
