     |      all have the same data types of ``category``,
     |      only ``c`` and ``d`` will be counted as one group
     |      since ``a`` doesn't have the same categories.
     |
     |      >>> df = pd.DataFrame({"a": [1], "b": ["2"], "c": [3], "d": [3]})
     |      >>> df = df.astype({"a": "category", "c": "category", "d": "category"})
     |      >>> df
