     |      because the maximum of a NaN and a float is a NaN.
     |      So, in the example, we set ``fill_value=0``,
     |      so the maximum value returned will be the value from some dataset.
     |
     |      >>> s1.combine(s2, max, fill_value=0)
     |      duck       30.0
     |      eagle     200.0
     |      falcon    345.0
     |      dtype: float64
